WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.138 --> 00:00:04.207
- What's up believe nation?

00:00:04.207 --> 00:00:06.620
I started the Mentor Me series
to try to learn from people

00:00:06.620 --> 00:00:09.549
who've done a lot more than us,
spend a little bit more time

00:00:09.549 --> 00:00:11.766
with them, and hopefully
some of their beliefs,

00:00:11.766 --> 00:00:14.878
their viewpoints, their
mindset, seeps into us

00:00:14.878 --> 00:00:17.851
to help us become the
best version of ourselves.

00:00:17.851 --> 00:00:19.839
So today we're going to learn
from Arnold Schwarzenegger

00:00:19.839 --> 00:00:22.207
and some of his most inspiring moments.

00:00:22.207 --> 00:00:23.542
Mentor me, Arnold.

00:00:23.542 --> 00:00:25.688
And as always guys, as
you're watching the videos,

00:00:25.688 --> 00:00:27.791
if you see something that
really resonates with you,

00:00:27.791 --> 00:00:29.507
please leave it in the comments below

00:00:29.507 --> 00:00:32.240
and put quotes around it so
other people can be inspired.

00:00:32.240 --> 00:00:34.034
And if you write it down,
it's much more likely

00:00:34.034 --> 00:00:36.617
to stick with yourself as well.

00:00:37.596 --> 00:00:40.429
(inspiring music)

00:00:49.454 --> 00:00:53.285
- The most important thing
is that you have a vision.

00:00:53.285 --> 00:00:54.766
That you have a goal.

00:00:54.766 --> 00:00:57.173
Because without that vision
and without that goal,

00:00:57.173 --> 00:00:59.292
again you're drifting
around and you're never

00:00:59.292 --> 00:01:00.589
going to end up anywhere.

00:01:00.589 --> 00:01:04.755
People don't become
successful just by accident.

00:01:04.755 --> 00:01:09.143
I mean maybe the guy that
found gold in California

00:01:09.143 --> 00:01:11.635
and started the gold rush,
but don't count on that.

00:01:11.635 --> 00:01:14.580
That's one in a lifetime
kind of situation.

00:01:14.580 --> 00:01:17.869
So you've got to really have
a specific goal, and to me,

00:01:17.869 --> 00:01:21.596
to have that vision that
I want to be Mr. Universe,

00:01:21.596 --> 00:01:24.477
that I want to be the greatest
body builder of all time,

00:01:24.477 --> 00:01:28.048
that was a great vision
and specifically to look

00:01:28.048 --> 00:01:30.169
like Reg Park and to be
up there on that stage

00:01:30.169 --> 00:01:33.887
and to lift the trophy overhead
and to win the championship

00:01:33.887 --> 00:01:35.754
over and over and over again.

00:01:35.754 --> 00:01:38.209
So that was a great goal,
you have to have a goal.

00:01:38.209 --> 00:01:40.241
Now it doesn't have to
be that specific goal,

00:01:40.241 --> 00:01:42.167
but it has to have some goal.

00:01:42.167 --> 00:01:44.900
This is why I always
recommend to people, sit down,

00:01:44.900 --> 00:01:47.236
take your time, and start thinking about

00:01:47.236 --> 00:01:49.528
why do you want to work out?

00:01:49.528 --> 00:01:50.757
What is your goal?

00:01:50.757 --> 00:01:53.525
And it can be as crazy
as it is, it could be

00:01:53.525 --> 00:01:55.587
I want to impress girls.

00:01:55.587 --> 00:01:59.494
If that's your goal, so be
it, but it motivates you.

00:01:59.494 --> 00:02:03.081
It could be that you're
emulating a certain body builder

00:02:03.081 --> 00:02:05.294
or a certain football
player or a certain boxer.

00:02:05.294 --> 00:02:08.836
Whatever it is, have those
pictures put all over the wall

00:02:08.836 --> 00:02:11.976
like I did when I was a kid,
I put pictures of Reg Park

00:02:11.976 --> 00:02:14.972
and of Sonny Liston,
of boxers, and of Ali,

00:02:14.972 --> 00:02:18.395
and of power lifters, and weight
lifters all over my bedroom

00:02:18.395 --> 00:02:22.780
in a wall so that every
day when I go to sleep,

00:02:22.780 --> 00:02:25.372
every day when I wake up,
I look at those pictures

00:02:25.372 --> 00:02:26.628
and they motivate me.

00:02:26.628 --> 00:02:29.976
You need that motivation and
therefore you have to kind of

00:02:29.976 --> 00:02:32.476
imprint in front of you all the time

00:02:32.476 --> 00:02:34.660
and you know exactly what you're chasing.

00:02:34.660 --> 00:02:37.941
This is why I always smiled
when I was in the gym.

00:02:37.941 --> 00:02:39.132
People always came up to me and says

00:02:39.132 --> 00:02:41.930
why are you smiling, you're
working out five hours a day.

00:02:41.930 --> 00:02:43.546
You're doing the same as the other guys,

00:02:43.546 --> 00:02:46.171
but the other guys have a
sour face, they're pissed off

00:02:46.171 --> 00:02:47.361
that they have to do another rep

00:02:47.361 --> 00:02:48.651
or another set or something.

00:02:48.651 --> 00:02:51.471
I looked forward to, I looked
forward to another thousand

00:02:51.471 --> 00:02:55.284
reps of sit ups, I looked
forward to another 500 pounds

00:02:55.284 --> 00:02:57.117
of leg press or squat.

00:02:58.235 --> 00:03:00.279
I looked forward doing more and more curls

00:03:00.279 --> 00:03:01.808
until my arms fall off.

00:03:01.808 --> 00:03:04.532
Why, because I knew that
every rep that I did

00:03:04.532 --> 00:03:07.325
and every set that I did and
more weights that I lifted,

00:03:07.325 --> 00:03:11.690
I get one step closer to turning
that vision into reality.

00:03:11.690 --> 00:03:14.758
So I was turned on by that, I was excited.

00:03:14.758 --> 00:03:16.728
I couldn't wait to get to the gym.

00:03:16.728 --> 00:03:20.938
When I used to do seminars
on how to become a champion

00:03:20.938 --> 00:03:25.273
I would always ask people why
do you want to be a champion?

00:03:25.273 --> 00:03:26.877
Or what do you want to accomplish?

00:03:26.877 --> 00:03:28.087
Why are you training?

00:03:28.087 --> 00:03:31.407
And if a guy will get up, and he will say,

00:03:31.407 --> 00:03:35.574
well I want to train because
I think that if I get muscular

00:03:38.021 --> 00:03:41.220
and I feel like I'm getting
the kind of definition

00:03:41.220 --> 00:03:44.958
then I maybe can enter a
body building competition.

00:03:44.958 --> 00:03:46.505
I said, sit down.

00:03:46.505 --> 00:03:50.078
Cause if you think this way,
you're going to be a loser.

00:03:50.078 --> 00:03:52.544
You're never going to make
it because there's no maybe.

00:03:52.544 --> 00:03:56.759
You got to get up and say,
I want to be a champion.

00:03:56.759 --> 00:03:59.113
And I do whatever it takes.

00:03:59.113 --> 00:04:00.806
The amount of hours it takes, the posing,

00:04:00.806 --> 00:04:02.661
the this, the that, the visualization.

00:04:02.661 --> 00:04:05.414
Looking at training footage,
looking at motivational books,

00:04:05.414 --> 00:04:08.494
reading this, whatever
it takes, I will do.

00:04:08.494 --> 00:04:11.197
That's the answer I want to hear from you.

00:04:11.197 --> 00:04:15.557
You can detect right away those
that are going to be shaky

00:04:15.557 --> 00:04:17.258
and that will fall behind.

00:04:17.258 --> 00:04:18.690
They will not go all the way.

00:04:18.690 --> 00:04:20.121
And those that are very hungry.

00:04:20.121 --> 00:04:22.095
And that hunger you have to
develop because you have to

00:04:22.095 --> 00:04:24.676
create a goal for yourself,
whatever that may be.

00:04:24.676 --> 00:04:28.015
A short-term goal and a
long-term goal and you got to go

00:04:28.015 --> 00:04:30.518
after that and if you do not see it,

00:04:30.518 --> 00:04:33.954
and if you do not believe
it, who else will?

00:04:33.954 --> 00:04:36.196
Don't be afraid to fail.

00:04:36.196 --> 00:04:40.363
Anything I've ever attempted,
I was always willing to fail.

00:04:42.032 --> 00:04:44.510
In the movie business I
remember they depict scripts.

00:04:44.510 --> 00:04:46.674
Many times you think
this is a winning script,

00:04:46.674 --> 00:04:48.309
but then of course you find out later on

00:04:48.309 --> 00:04:50.345
when you do the movie that it didn't work

00:04:50.345 --> 00:04:52.779
and the movie goes in the toilet.

00:04:52.779 --> 00:04:55.863
Now we have seen my
movies, I mean, Red Sonja,

00:04:55.863 --> 00:04:58.685
Hercules in New York, Last Action Hero.

00:04:58.685 --> 00:05:00.770
Those movies went in the toilet.

00:05:00.770 --> 00:05:04.184
But that's okay, because at
the same time I made movies

00:05:04.184 --> 00:05:07.350
like Terminator and Conan
and True Lies and Predator

00:05:07.350 --> 00:05:09.515
and Twins that went through the roof.

00:05:09.515 --> 00:05:12.199
So you can't always
win but don't be afraid

00:05:12.199 --> 00:05:13.909
of making decisions.

00:05:13.909 --> 00:05:16.317
You can't be paralyzed by fear or failure

00:05:16.317 --> 00:05:18.511
or you will never push yourself.

00:05:18.511 --> 00:05:20.766
You keep pushing because
you believe in yourself

00:05:20.766 --> 00:05:24.131
and in your vision and you
know that it is the right thing

00:05:24.131 --> 00:05:25.658
to do and success will come.

00:05:25.658 --> 00:05:28.286
So don't be afraid to fail.

00:05:28.286 --> 00:05:31.469
- In one word, one word only,
how did a small town boy

00:05:31.469 --> 00:05:35.519
from Austria become one of the
most famous people on earth?

00:05:35.519 --> 00:05:37.332
- Why do you want me
to say it in one word?

00:05:37.332 --> 00:05:38.543
(laughter)

00:05:38.543 --> 00:05:40.272
- One word, Arnold.

00:05:40.272 --> 00:05:42.142
- I don't stay with your rules.

00:05:42.142 --> 00:05:43.430
Dream.

00:05:43.430 --> 00:05:44.287
- Dream.

00:05:44.287 --> 00:05:45.134
- Dream.

00:05:45.134 --> 00:05:49.102
I was poor because I didn't have anything.

00:05:49.102 --> 00:05:51.554
I had no money, I had
no things, we had no TV,

00:05:51.554 --> 00:05:53.504
we had no refrigerator,
we had nothing as kids.

00:05:53.504 --> 00:05:55.508
But I was rich because I had a dream.

00:05:55.508 --> 00:05:56.341
- You had a dream.

00:05:56.341 --> 00:06:00.012
- I had a dream of becoming
the greatest body builder

00:06:00.012 --> 00:06:02.172
and I had a dream to use body building

00:06:02.172 --> 00:06:04.421
as a means to get into films.

00:06:04.421 --> 00:06:08.365
But I had no idea that it
would go as far as it did.

00:06:08.365 --> 00:06:12.183
That it would go beyond the
body roles, beyond the muscles

00:06:12.183 --> 00:06:15.663
and into movies like Terminator,
Predator, End of Days,

00:06:15.663 --> 00:06:16.675
and stuff like that.

00:06:16.675 --> 00:06:19.814
That was like, you know, I had
to kind of reinvent my dream

00:06:19.814 --> 00:06:21.412
after I achieved that.

00:06:21.412 --> 00:06:23.980
- Okay, but this dream of body
building, we'll come to that,

00:06:23.980 --> 00:06:25.730
but there must have been a
time in your life before that

00:06:25.730 --> 00:06:27.935
when you didn't have thoughts
of body building at all.

00:06:27.935 --> 00:06:29.054
What sort of child were you?

00:06:29.054 --> 00:06:31.451
- Well I grew up in
Austria, I was born after

00:06:31.451 --> 00:06:34.937
the second World War in
1947, it was poverty.

00:06:34.937 --> 00:06:37.563
There was no food around, really nothing.

00:06:37.563 --> 00:06:40.262
And I think that was the
reason why I developed

00:06:40.262 --> 00:06:44.429
such a tremendous desire to
get out of there and a desire

00:06:46.225 --> 00:06:49.473
to make it in life, to achieve big things.

00:06:49.473 --> 00:06:52.840
And then when I learned in
school later on about America

00:06:52.840 --> 00:06:56.076
and about the skyscrapers,
the big freeways, the big cars

00:06:56.076 --> 00:06:58.170
and all that, I said Miss Avine, I want to

00:06:58.170 --> 00:06:59.663
be part of this big thing.

00:06:59.663 --> 00:07:02.225
Everyone has a problem with time.

00:07:02.225 --> 00:07:05.642
But the day is 24 hours and we sleep six.

00:07:08.353 --> 00:07:10.193
Now I know there are
some out there that say

00:07:10.193 --> 00:07:12.452
Oh woah, woah, woah, woah, I need eight.

00:07:12.452 --> 00:07:14.660
Well I say, just sleep a little faster

00:07:14.660 --> 00:07:18.622
because the bottom line is
we have six hours of sleep,

00:07:18.622 --> 00:07:21.939
24 hours are available so you
have 18 hours now available

00:07:21.939 --> 00:07:26.022
to your work, your family,
your hobbies, and also

00:07:28.247 --> 00:07:31.382
to learn something new
or to do something new.

00:07:31.382 --> 00:07:34.252
Which could easily be that you
want to learn a new language,

00:07:34.252 --> 00:07:37.896
or that you want to read
as a New Years resolution,

00:07:37.896 --> 00:07:40.231
have to read a book every week or you say

00:07:40.231 --> 00:07:42.507
I'm going to go and re-shape my body.

00:07:42.507 --> 00:07:44.498
So you're going to go and take this hour

00:07:44.498 --> 00:07:46.562
out of your schedule and
say I'm going to train

00:07:46.562 --> 00:07:47.973
an hour every day.

00:07:47.973 --> 00:07:50.897
So this is for most
people a huge challenge

00:07:50.897 --> 00:07:53.008
but it is totally doable, I can tell them.

00:07:53.008 --> 00:07:55.117
Because the kind of things that I did

00:07:55.117 --> 00:07:56.708
when I came to this country.

00:07:56.708 --> 00:07:59.728
I mean, I went to school, I
was working in construction,

00:07:59.728 --> 00:08:03.166
I was working out five
hours a day, I was taking

00:08:03.166 --> 00:08:06.576
acting classes from eight
o'clock at night to 12 midnight.

00:08:06.576 --> 00:08:08.877
I was doing all of those things.

00:08:08.877 --> 00:08:13.725
I wanted to make sure that
out of the 24 hours of the day

00:08:13.725 --> 00:08:16.427
that I don't waste one single hour.

00:08:16.427 --> 00:08:18.139
Those hours were too precious.

00:08:18.139 --> 00:08:19.556
And so then I just want to tell people

00:08:19.556 --> 00:08:21.820
don't give me this thing,
I have a difficult time

00:08:21.820 --> 00:08:24.410
with the time, and I don't have
time for this, none of that.

00:08:24.410 --> 00:08:26.869
You have time, you make the time.

00:08:26.869 --> 00:08:30.231
When you're a competitive
athlete, you learn very quickly

00:08:30.231 --> 00:08:33.014
how strong you are or
how energetic you are.

00:08:33.014 --> 00:08:34.141
All of those things.

00:08:34.141 --> 00:08:36.589
But, it could very well be
that there's a lot of people

00:08:36.589 --> 00:08:39.597
who have an equally as
good a body as you have.

00:08:39.597 --> 00:08:42.620
That performs just as
well, that is as muscular,

00:08:42.620 --> 00:08:45.521
the same body building, that
has exactly the same kind of,

00:08:45.521 --> 00:08:48.030
you know, proportions
and all of those things.

00:08:48.030 --> 00:08:50.953
So the question really is is
what puts you over the top?

00:08:50.953 --> 00:08:54.416
It is the mind that
really creates the body.

00:08:54.416 --> 00:08:56.721
It's the mind that makes
you really work out

00:08:56.721 --> 00:08:58.349
the four or five hours a day.

00:08:58.349 --> 00:09:02.009
It is the mind that
visualizes of what the body

00:09:02.009 --> 00:09:04.340
ought to look like as
the finished product.

00:09:04.340 --> 00:09:08.136
The body is very important,
but the mind is more important

00:09:08.136 --> 00:09:09.236
than the body.

00:09:09.236 --> 00:09:12.399
You have to visualize what
that body ought to look like

00:09:12.399 --> 00:09:13.678
in order to make it win.

00:09:13.678 --> 00:09:15.740
Because that's what creates then the will.

00:09:15.740 --> 00:09:18.460
The will that you need to
go to the gym every day.

00:09:18.460 --> 00:09:21.318
The will that makes you
go into the four steps.

00:09:21.318 --> 00:09:24.830
The will that makes you go
beyond and you do your 500 pound

00:09:24.830 --> 00:09:28.199
reps and the squats and
you can't do another rep,

00:09:28.199 --> 00:09:30.880
and your body is shaking,
it's the will that makes you

00:09:30.880 --> 00:09:34.030
go one more time down and
struggle up one more time.

00:09:34.030 --> 00:09:36.560
And since all of this is the mental aspect

00:09:36.560 --> 00:09:38.876
that motivates you, and
that makes the difference

00:09:38.876 --> 00:09:42.481
of you being in the gym full
of joy and looking forward

00:09:42.481 --> 00:09:46.189
to doing that extra rep and
looking forward to doing

00:09:46.189 --> 00:09:48.199
those extra hundred reps and the sit-ups

00:09:48.199 --> 00:09:50.320
and working past the pain periods.

00:09:50.320 --> 00:09:52.565
That's all is the mind,
that's not the body.

00:09:52.565 --> 00:09:55.873
So this is why I think
the body is very important

00:09:55.873 --> 00:09:58.875
but the mind is more
important than the body.

00:09:58.875 --> 00:10:01.597
You have so many rules
in life about everything.

00:10:01.597 --> 00:10:04.320
I say break the rules, not
the law, but break the rules.

00:10:04.320 --> 00:10:08.298
My wife has a t-shirt, my
wife has a t-shirt that says

00:10:08.298 --> 00:10:11.371
Well behaved women rarely make history.

00:10:11.371 --> 00:10:14.424
Well you know, I don't
want to burst her bubble,

00:10:14.424 --> 00:10:16.690
but the same is true with men.

00:10:16.690 --> 00:10:19.521
It is impossible to be a
maverick or a true original

00:10:19.521 --> 00:10:21.967
if you're too well-behaved and don't want

00:10:21.967 --> 00:10:23.430
to break the rules.

00:10:23.430 --> 00:10:25.629
You have to think outside the box.

00:10:25.629 --> 00:10:26.613
That's what I believe.

00:10:26.613 --> 00:10:29.444
After all, what is the
point of being on this earth

00:10:29.444 --> 00:10:31.582
if all you want to do
is be liked by everyone

00:10:31.582 --> 00:10:32.828
and avoid trouble.

00:10:32.828 --> 00:10:35.746
The only way that I ever got any place

00:10:35.746 --> 00:10:38.183
was by breaking some of the rules.

00:10:38.183 --> 00:10:41.264
After all, I remember that
after I was finished with my

00:10:41.264 --> 00:10:43.640
body building career, I
wanted to get into acting,

00:10:43.640 --> 00:10:46.140
and I wanted to be a star in films.

00:10:46.140 --> 00:10:48.534
You can imagine what the agents said

00:10:48.534 --> 00:10:50.841
when I went to meet all those agents.

00:10:50.841 --> 00:10:53.099
Every one had the same
line, that it can't be done.

00:10:53.099 --> 00:10:55.322
The rules are different here.

00:10:55.322 --> 00:10:58.496
Says look at your body, you
have this huge, monstrous body,

00:10:58.496 --> 00:11:01.631
overly developed, that
doesn't fit into the movies.

00:11:01.631 --> 00:11:02.998
You don't understand.

00:11:02.998 --> 00:11:05.828
This was 20 years ago,
the Hercules movies.

00:11:05.828 --> 00:11:09.020
Now there is the little guys
today and Dustin Hoffman,

00:11:09.020 --> 00:11:11.973
Woody Allen, Jack Nicholson,

00:11:11.973 --> 00:11:14.606
before he gained weight
of course, that is.

00:11:14.606 --> 00:11:17.351
But anyway, those are the guys that win.

00:11:17.351 --> 00:11:19.433
And the agent also
complained about my accent.

00:11:19.433 --> 00:11:22.296
He says no one ever became a
star with an accent like that.

00:11:22.296 --> 00:11:24.370
Especially not with a
German accent and yes,

00:11:24.370 --> 00:11:27.797
I can imagine with your name,
Arnold Schwarzen-schnitzle,

00:11:27.797 --> 00:11:30.097
or whatever the name is, on a billboard.

00:11:30.097 --> 00:11:32.054
Yeah that's going to draw a
lot of tickets and sell a lot

00:11:32.054 --> 00:11:33.613
of tickets, yeah right.

00:11:33.613 --> 00:11:36.264
So this is the kind of
negative attitude they had,

00:11:36.264 --> 00:11:38.759
but I didn't listen to those rules.

00:11:38.759 --> 00:11:40.460
Even though they were very
nice and they said look,

00:11:40.460 --> 00:11:42.017
we can get you some good parts.

00:11:42.017 --> 00:11:46.670
We can get you to playing
a wrestler or bouncer.

00:11:46.670 --> 00:11:48.707
Oh, maybe with your German
accent we can get you

00:11:48.707 --> 00:11:51.544
to be a Nazi officer in Hogan's Heroes

00:11:51.544 --> 00:11:52.948
or something like that.

00:11:52.948 --> 00:11:55.475
But, you know, I didn't
listen to all those.

00:11:55.475 --> 00:11:57.788
Those were their rules, not my rules.

00:11:57.788 --> 00:12:01.059
I was convinced I could do
it, that if I worked as hard

00:12:01.059 --> 00:12:03.531
as I did in body building,
five hours a day.

00:12:03.531 --> 00:12:05.578
And I started getting to
work, I started taking

00:12:05.578 --> 00:12:09.613
acting classes, took English
classes, took speech classes,

00:12:09.613 --> 00:12:13.530
dialogue classes, accent
removal classes I even took.

00:12:13.530 --> 00:12:17.697
I remember running around,
a fine wine grows on a vine.

00:12:18.614 --> 00:12:21.414
Is it because Germans have
difficulties with the F and the W

00:12:21.414 --> 00:12:24.875
and the V, so fine wine grows on a vine.

00:12:24.875 --> 00:12:27.588
I know what some of you now
say is that hope that Arnold

00:12:27.588 --> 00:12:29.787
got his money back, but
let me tell you something.

00:12:29.787 --> 00:12:32.026
I had a good time doing those things

00:12:32.026 --> 00:12:34.415
and they really helped me
and finally I broke through.

00:12:34.415 --> 00:12:37.008
I broke through and I started
getting the first parts

00:12:37.008 --> 00:12:41.344
in TV, Streets of San Francisco,
Lucille Ball hired me.

00:12:41.344 --> 00:12:43.749
I made Pumping Iron, Stay Hungry.

00:12:43.749 --> 00:12:47.916
And then I got the big break
in Conan the Barbarian.

00:12:49.016 --> 00:12:51.844
And there the director say if
we didn't have Schwarzenegger

00:12:51.844 --> 00:12:53.722
we would have to build one.

00:12:53.722 --> 00:12:54.894
Now think about that.

00:12:54.894 --> 00:12:58.727
And then, when I did
Terminator, I'll be back,

00:13:00.935 --> 00:13:05.006
became one of the most famous
lines in movie history.

00:13:05.006 --> 00:13:07.778
All because of my crazy accent.

00:13:07.778 --> 00:13:10.671
Now think about it, the
things that the agents said

00:13:10.671 --> 00:13:14.005
would be totally a detriment
and would be impossible

00:13:14.005 --> 00:13:17.438
for me to get a job all of a
sudden became as asset for me.

00:13:17.438 --> 00:13:20.075
All of those things, my accent,
my body, and everything.

00:13:20.075 --> 00:13:21.677
So it just shows to you, never listen

00:13:21.677 --> 00:13:23.473
that you can't do something.

00:13:23.473 --> 00:13:25.603
And you have to work your way up,

00:13:25.603 --> 00:13:27.648
of course, run for something else first.

00:13:27.648 --> 00:13:32.283
I mean it was the same, and
I when I ran for governor,

00:13:32.283 --> 00:13:34.017
the same lines, that you
have to work your way up,

00:13:34.017 --> 00:13:35.113
it can't be done.

00:13:35.113 --> 00:13:37.480
And then of course, I ran
for governor, and the rest,

00:13:37.480 --> 00:13:38.556
of course, is history.

00:13:38.556 --> 00:13:41.047
They said you have to start
with a small job as mayor.

00:13:41.047 --> 00:13:42.879
And then there's assemblyman, and then

00:13:42.879 --> 00:13:45.683
there is lieutenant governor,
and then as governor.

00:13:45.683 --> 00:13:48.267
And they said that's the way
it works in a political career.

00:13:48.267 --> 00:13:50.702
I said I'm not interested
in a political career.

00:13:50.702 --> 00:13:52.439
I want to be a public servant.

00:13:52.439 --> 00:13:54.791
I want to fix California's
problems and bring people

00:13:54.791 --> 00:13:56.730
together and bring the parties together.

00:13:56.730 --> 00:13:59.788
So like I said, I decided to
run, I didn't pay attention

00:13:59.788 --> 00:14:03.652
to the rules and I made it
and the rest is history.

00:14:03.652 --> 00:14:05.321
- Thank you guys so much for watching,

00:14:05.321 --> 00:14:07.333
I'd love to know, what did
you think of this video?

00:14:07.333 --> 00:14:09.327
What did you learn from
Arnold that's going to have

00:14:09.327 --> 00:14:12.203
the biggest immediate impact
on your life or your business?

00:14:12.203 --> 00:14:14.544
Which one was your favorite clip and why?

00:14:14.544 --> 00:14:16.655
Please leave it in the
comments below and I'm going to

00:14:16.655 --> 00:14:17.955
join in the discussion.

00:14:17.955 --> 00:14:19.259
Finally, I want to give a quick shout out

00:14:19.259 --> 00:14:20.516
to Vincent Montello.

00:14:20.516 --> 00:14:22.767
Vincent, thank you so much for
picking up a copy of my book,

00:14:22.767 --> 00:14:25.617
Your One Word, and making
that book summary video

00:14:25.617 --> 00:14:27.927
on your YouTube channel,
I really, really, really

00:14:27.927 --> 00:14:29.359
appreciate the support.

00:14:29.359 --> 00:14:33.526
- Today, we are covering Evan
Carmichael's Your One Word.

00:14:34.708 --> 00:14:36.399
- So thank you guys again for watching.

00:14:36.399 --> 00:14:39.440
I believe in you, I hope you
continue to believe in yourself

00:14:39.440 --> 00:14:41.287
and whatever your one word is.

00:14:41.287 --> 00:14:43.704
Much love, I'll see you soon.

